request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands  (The request needs a new Command variant in types, and commands needs a pure clear() function plus parseArgs/run support. Todo has no 'completed' field. Its completion flag is `done`, which the existing complete command sets, so I read "completed" as done === true.)
round 1: owners types=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 20 vitest tests pass. The manifest now shows the { kind: "clear" } Command variant in types and the exported clear(todos) in commands. That covers the request: clear removes todos with done === true (the Todo type's completed flag), is handled by parseArgs and run, and leaves existing behaviour unchanged.)

